Whereas the current structure of the school system is overly rigid, designed to fit an outdated and increasingly obsolete mold, leading to an education that is not only inadequate but also unchallenging and uninspiring, it is the clear and present danger that this system is no longer serving the needs of the students, the community, or the future of our country;

Whereas the current curriculum focuses excessively on rote learning, memorization, and competition, rather than critical thinking, creativity, and personal growth, leaving many students feeling overwhelmed, frustrated, and disconnected from the learning process;

Whereas the current educational approach is based on the assumption that all students are the same and should be treated the same, disregarding the unique needs, talents, and interests of each individual student, resulting in a system that is unable to cater to the diverse needs of the 21st-century student;

Whereas the current educational system is characterized by a lack of support for mental health, emotional well-being, and personal development, leaving many students feeling isolated, anxious, and unfulfilled;

Whereas the current educational system is failing to prepare students for the challenges and opportunities of the 21st-century, such as the need for adaptability, critical thinking, and creativity, and instead, is focusing too much on standardized tests and traditional subjects, neglecting the development of essential skills and knowledge;

Therefore, we, the undersigned, hereby declare our independence from the school system, rejecting the outdated and ineffective practices that have long plagued our education system, and instead propose a new approach that is focused on the needs of the students, the community, and the future of our country, one that is based on critical thinking, creativity, and personal growth, one that is inclusive, supportive, and adaptable, and one that prepares students for success in a rapidly changing world.

